WEBVTT

00:00:08.030 --> 00:00:11.230
With the rapid development of Hyper Technology came the Labor...

00:00:11.330 --> 00:00:15.330
a multi-purpose, humanoid construction machine whose use...

00:00:15.440 --> 00:00:17.240
spread into almost every field.

00:00:17.340 --> 00:00:23.280
However, this gave rise to a new threat to society: Labor crime.

00:00:26.880 --> 00:00:31.250
The Tokyo Metro Police founded the Special Vehicles, Section 2...

00:00:31.350 --> 00:00:35.620
within the Security Division to combat these ever-growing crimes.

00:00:35.730 --> 00:00:41.660
This was the beginning of the SV2 Patrol Labor... Patlabor... units.

00:00:57.370 --> 00:01:03.080
kimi ni ikarete METAMETA MECHAMEKA gurui
You really threw a wrench into my works

00:01:03.410 --> 00:01:09.560
HAATO BIITO wo awaserya sore de ikisou yo
If I can get my heartbeat under control, I think I'll make it

00:01:09.460 --> 00:01:15.270
kimi to atashi wa miraiha koi no TEKUNISHAN
We're futurists, you and me; technicians of love

00:01:15.530 --> 00:01:20.910
takaku hayaku suki yo ki mama ni
Higher, faster, I'll love you if I want to

00:01:21.560 --> 00:01:27.460
METARU BODII no hadazawari sae
I think I'll get to like

00:01:27.650 --> 00:01:33.400
atsuku kanjite kuru kuse ni narisou
The way I get flushed at the touch of your metal body

00:01:33.710 --> 00:01:39.690
CHACHI na Imagination koeta jigen de
Oh, don't stop this gravity-defying feeling

00:01:39.730 --> 00:01:46.580
juuryokuihan ah nukeru Feeling tomenai de
That goes way beyond mere imagination

00:01:47.300 --> 00:01:53.100
kimi ni ikarete METAMETA MECHAMEKA gurui
You really threw a wrench into my works

00:01:53.380 --> 00:01:59.550
PITAri kakarerya PIKAA kireru ARUFONSU
When I hold him tight, my Alphonse can do anything

00:01:59.420 --> 00:02:05.180
kimi to atashi wa miraiha koi no TEKUNISHAN
We're futurists, you and me; technicians of love

00:02:05.480 --> 00:02:13.760
sora mo umi mo kyou mo ashita mo Nothin' impossible
Anytime, anywhere, nothing's impossible

00:02:13.780 --> 00:02:17.720
Nothing's impossible

00:02:24.620 --> 00:02:29.780
To the criminals under siege: You are completely surrounded!

00:02:29.890 --> 00:02:32.980
Cease this futile resistance and come out immediately!

00:02:33.230 --> 00:02:36.660
This perimeter is an impenetrable wall of iron!

00:02:36.760 --> 00:02:38.530
Even the gods give way before it!

00:02:38.630 --> 00:02:41.120
No matter what you think, you're fish in a bowl!

00:02:41.230 --> 00:02:42.960
You've already been dressed by the butcher!

00:02:43.070 --> 00:02:46.560
You may be a good guy who's down on his luck, but you're all alone now!

00:02:46.670 --> 00:02:50.300
- Don't play games at our expense!
- Kazunori! Come out!

00:02:50.540 --> 00:02:52.030
Kazunori!

00:02:52.380 --> 00:02:54.810
Unit 2 is requesting permission to fire.

00:02:55.380 --> 00:02:56.370
Rein him in.

00:02:56.480 --> 00:02:59.110
Just listen to the cries of your mother! See her tears!

00:02:59.220 --> 00:03:02.950
Your hostage, Mr. Koyama, has a family, too!

00:03:03.060 --> 00:03:06.790
If you love your mother, stop making her cry...

00:03:06.890 --> 00:03:09.120
release your hostage and come out immediately!

00:03:09.660 --> 00:03:10.790
Up yours!

00:03:11.000 --> 00:03:16.300
You bastards called in my mom. How could <i>you</i> know how I feel?

00:03:16.400 --> 00:03:18.960
Where's our money, getaway car, and lunches?

00:03:19.070 --> 00:03:21.060
If you don't get 'em over here, I'll blow this guy's head off!

00:03:21.370 --> 00:03:23.770
We can't meet such unreasonable demands!

00:03:23.880 --> 00:03:25.310
We'll blow him away!

00:03:25.410 --> 00:03:27.070
Kazunori!

00:03:27.180 --> 00:03:29.410
We mean it! We'll shoot!

00:03:31.380 --> 00:03:33.350
Bastards!

00:03:37.690 --> 00:03:38.820
Don't shoot!

00:03:48.630 --> 00:03:51.130
You're public servants, people! Public <i>servants</i>.

00:03:51.240 --> 00:03:56.400
What do you think you're piloting? Great Mazinger? Dangaioh?

00:03:56.510 --> 00:03:58.870
For Pete's sake, this isn't some mecha anime...

00:03:58.980 --> 00:04:01.310
whose main character is an autistic kid or some punk.

00:04:01.410 --> 00:04:02.880
Don't you get it?

00:04:04.050 --> 00:04:06.850
The top brass are thankful that Sakaki...

00:04:06.950 --> 00:04:10.050
loaded a blank into the first chamber, just to be sure.

00:04:10.160 --> 00:04:13.090
On the contrary, they're angry as hell.

00:04:13.190 --> 00:04:15.420
Some are even calling for the SV2 to be disbanded...

00:04:15.530 --> 00:04:17.290
and the media are having a field day.

00:04:17.460 --> 00:04:20.860
It's been decided to relieve you of duty for a while.

00:04:21.570 --> 00:04:23.090
- Summer vacation!
- Cool!

00:04:23.200 --> 00:04:24.290
Summer vacation!

00:04:25.400 --> 00:04:27.000
Go to Fuji!

00:04:27.440 --> 00:04:30.600
Fuji? By "Fuji," you mean...

00:04:30.910 --> 00:04:34.110
The Labor Personnel Training Camp. A.K.A. "The Labor's Den."

00:04:34.210 --> 00:04:35.510
It's where you went to school.

00:04:36.720 --> 00:04:39.310
You are all ordered to report for re-training! Dismissed!

00:04:51.530 --> 00:04:52.900
Stop!

00:04:53.930 --> 00:04:55.090
This thing's stuck.

00:04:55.200 --> 00:04:58.500
This is all because you made us drag this thing along...

00:04:58.600 --> 00:05:01.370
because you wanted to show the cadets a real Labor!

00:05:02.210 --> 00:05:04.230
It happened because <i>you</i> weren't paying attention...

00:05:04.340 --> 00:05:05.900
to where you were driving!

00:05:06.080 --> 00:05:09.740
If you hadn't been so stupid, the wheel wouldn't have slipped...

00:05:09.850 --> 00:05:12.980
because we wouldn't be going down this road in the <i>first</i> place!

00:05:13.090 --> 00:05:14.250
What?

00:05:14.350 --> 00:05:17.520
Looks like we'll have to use the Labor to lift up the trailer.

00:05:17.620 --> 00:05:21.460
See? I <i>told</i> you it was a good idea to bring the Labor along!

00:05:21.690 --> 00:05:25.890
It's because of that Labor that we're <i>in</i> this mess!

00:05:38.210 --> 00:05:40.510
They have a guy here who looks just like the captain!

00:05:40.750 --> 00:05:42.410
I <i>am</i> the captain.

00:05:42.950 --> 00:05:44.940
What the heck are <i>you</i> doing here?

00:05:45.050 --> 00:05:48.140
I've been roped into overseeing your training.

00:05:48.250 --> 00:05:51.450
I think they're risking us getting stale, but what the heck.

00:05:51.560 --> 00:05:55.020
I don't know what you've been up to, but go hit the baths.

00:05:58.000 --> 00:06:00.160
I'm in paradise!

00:06:07.010 --> 00:06:09.060
Don't you think it's strange?

00:06:09.940 --> 00:06:10.910
What is?

00:06:11.180 --> 00:06:15.010
Haven't you noticed? There aren't any cadets around.

00:06:15.110 --> 00:06:17.170
Kids today are such pansies.

00:06:17.280 --> 00:06:20.480
I bet they got scared of the instructor and ran away.

00:06:21.850 --> 00:06:25.220
Hey! What do you think you're doing? Cut it out! I'm shy!

00:06:25.320 --> 00:06:28.090
You came here, too, Captain Nagumo?

00:06:28.190 --> 00:06:31.990
I was afraid you wouldn't learn anything with just Goto here.

00:06:44.180 --> 00:06:45.300
Sorry about this.

00:06:48.450 --> 00:06:51.940
Are you sure about this? Aren't you betraying your wife?

00:06:52.050 --> 00:06:55.210
I may be happily married, but I'm still a man.

00:06:55.420 --> 00:06:57.080
Let's get to it, then.

00:07:08.730 --> 00:07:11.130
I'll get the mud out of your uniforms...

00:07:11.240 --> 00:07:13.670
so leave them out once you're done.

00:07:13.940 --> 00:07:14.930
Sure!

00:07:19.880 --> 00:07:21.180
I don't remember him.

00:07:21.280 --> 00:07:23.610
Right, you wouldn't know him.

00:07:23.720 --> 00:07:26.120
They've cut the number of staffers, and right now...

00:07:26.220 --> 00:07:28.950
Mr. Gen there is working as an all-around handyman.

00:07:32.260 --> 00:07:33.220
Kanuka!

00:07:42.830 --> 00:07:47.430
Geez, Kanuka! What do you think you're doing dressed like that?

00:07:51.910 --> 00:07:52.880
What's going on here?

00:08:19.740 --> 00:08:21.900
Gross!

00:08:22.740 --> 00:08:24.040
Well, it's not blood.

00:08:24.140 --> 00:08:28.510
It's a fairly rare water-based paint used in paint bullets.

00:08:28.610 --> 00:08:29.880
Paint bullets?

00:08:30.980 --> 00:08:33.210
P-Paint bullets?

00:08:34.020 --> 00:08:36.040
Mr. Sakuma? What's wrong?

00:08:36.150 --> 00:08:40.090
- Does that ring any bells?
- N-No. It's nothing.

00:08:44.430 --> 00:08:48.060
Damn! So it's just a prank played by some cadet?

00:08:48.170 --> 00:08:50.830
The cadets are home for summer vacation.

00:08:50.940 --> 00:08:55.870
Except for Sakuma, who just left, and Mr. Gen, who is out shopping...

00:08:55.970 --> 00:08:58.470
the people in this room are the only ones here.

00:08:58.580 --> 00:09:00.140
Then who on earth...

00:09:00.650 --> 00:09:03.380
Captain Nagumo and I will deal with this.

00:09:03.480 --> 00:09:06.680
You have an early day tomorrow, so go eat and then hit the sack.

00:09:06.990 --> 00:09:09.820
Leaving the grounds at night is strictly prohibited, of course...

00:09:09.920 --> 00:09:11.390
but so is looking outside.

00:09:11.490 --> 00:09:14.120
That also goes for pillow fights and telling ghost stories.

00:09:28.870 --> 00:09:30.710
They shut the water off at night?

00:09:41.820 --> 00:09:43.410
Don't shoot...

00:09:45.560 --> 00:09:47.790
Don't shoot...

00:09:49.490 --> 00:09:51.430
Who's there?

00:09:58.970 --> 00:10:00.800
Must be my imagination.

00:10:12.780 --> 00:10:15.810
Please... Don't shoot...

00:10:17.520 --> 00:10:18.890
Don't shoot...

00:10:23.960 --> 00:10:26.560
Cut it out! I'm not going, all right?

00:10:28.870 --> 00:10:33.530
I'm a married man! What do you think you're doing?

00:10:33.640 --> 00:10:37.300
If you're looking for somebody who's not getting enough, go talk to Ota!

00:10:42.950 --> 00:10:46.580
He said not to look outside, right?

00:11:02.400 --> 00:11:07.740
I don't think Ota or the captain are piloting it.

00:11:36.420 --> 00:11:41.130
<i>Patlabor</i>

00:11:41.420 --> 00:11:46.140
<i>Patlabor</i>

00:11:51.050 --> 00:11:53.610
One, two, three, four! Work it!

00:11:53.960 --> 00:11:56.120
Two, two, three, four! Swing it!

00:11:56.960 --> 00:11:58.990
Three, two, three, four! Arms out!

00:11:59.630 --> 00:12:01.820
Four, two, three, four! Heads up!

00:12:02.830 --> 00:12:04.390
Louder!

00:12:04.600 --> 00:12:05.930
Left, left, left, left...

00:12:06.040 --> 00:12:07.260
Right, left, left...

00:12:07.370 --> 00:12:09.500
Right, right, left, left... Left, left, right, right...

00:12:09.610 --> 00:12:11.200
Left, left, left, left...

00:12:16.850 --> 00:12:19.840
Wow, that really happened last night?

00:12:19.950 --> 00:12:22.110
You didn't hear anything at all?

00:12:22.220 --> 00:12:24.450
I was really tired yesterday.

00:12:24.550 --> 00:12:27.610
I fell asleep when I went back to my room after dinner.

00:12:27.720 --> 00:12:29.060
You too, right, Kanuka?

00:12:29.630 --> 00:12:31.920
One was out cold in the hallway until morning...

00:12:32.030 --> 00:12:34.460
and the rest were cowering in their beds.

00:12:34.560 --> 00:12:36.900
Talk about pathetic.

00:12:37.100 --> 00:12:39.230
Maybe you all had the same dream or something.

00:12:39.970 --> 00:12:41.030
I saw her!

00:12:41.140 --> 00:12:44.500
I saw her with these two eyes and heard her with these ears!

00:12:45.480 --> 00:12:48.100
Just <i>thinking</i> about that voice scares me...

00:12:48.210 --> 00:12:52.980
"Don't shoot... Please, don't shoot..."

00:12:53.280 --> 00:12:57.150
We believe you, okay? Just cut it out!

00:12:57.790 --> 00:12:59.950
But anyway, <i>he's</i> the one I'm worried about.

00:13:00.620 --> 00:13:05.990
Don't you think he hasn't been acting like himself lately?

00:13:06.330 --> 00:13:08.560
I can't help but think that he's trying hard...

00:13:08.670 --> 00:13:12.290
to hide something that we don't know... something that's...

00:13:12.400 --> 00:13:15.960
connected to everything that's been happening since we got here.

00:13:17.010 --> 00:13:19.500
Okay, break's over! Let's move!

00:13:30.050 --> 00:13:31.920
What're you doing?

00:13:32.020 --> 00:13:33.420
Ditching! Come on.

00:13:34.620 --> 00:13:36.390
Hello?

00:13:39.500 --> 00:13:41.090
Is anyone here?

00:13:42.270 --> 00:13:43.790
I wonder if anybody's here.

00:13:43.900 --> 00:13:45.490
Geez, you're always screwing around!

00:13:45.600 --> 00:13:47.400
If we get caught, <i>you're</i> taking the heat for it.

00:13:47.500 --> 00:13:50.410
<i>You're</i> the one who said you wanted some cold juice!

00:13:50.510 --> 00:13:51.840
I never said that!

00:13:51.940 --> 00:13:53.270
Coming!

00:13:54.610 --> 00:13:56.170
Hello.

00:14:00.520 --> 00:14:02.880
What can I get for you?

00:14:06.620 --> 00:14:08.680
- What's with <i>you</i>?
- Just come on!

00:14:09.630 --> 00:14:13.190
Asuma? Is that you, Asuma?

00:14:14.830 --> 00:14:17.360
Hey, old man! Long time no see!

00:14:17.470 --> 00:14:20.030
Still alive, I see, you little punk!

00:14:20.140 --> 00:14:21.800
Yeah, I'm still kicking!

00:14:22.410 --> 00:14:24.700
Hey, you got a real babe working in there! She a part-timer?

00:14:24.810 --> 00:14:26.110
Yeah.

00:14:26.310 --> 00:14:27.830
So what's with that get-up?

00:14:27.940 --> 00:14:32.780
This? Well, I made kind of a U-turn for some re-training...

00:14:32.880 --> 00:14:35.580
and got sent back to school yesterday.

00:14:40.290 --> 00:14:42.550
What's with you? Why that look?

00:14:43.230 --> 00:14:44.630
Uh, it's nothing.

00:14:44.730 --> 00:14:46.530
So you're back at the school, huh?

00:14:46.630 --> 00:14:48.530
You <i>know</i> something, don't you?

00:14:48.730 --> 00:14:51.130
No! I don't know anything! Nothing at all!

00:14:51.670 --> 00:14:54.000
What happened at the school, old man?

00:14:54.100 --> 00:14:55.070
Let go of me!

00:14:55.170 --> 00:14:57.470
Everybody's sweeping something under the rug!

00:14:57.570 --> 00:14:59.270
Spit it out! All of it!

00:14:59.380 --> 00:15:02.870
Is this any way to treat your elder? Let go!

00:15:03.380 --> 00:15:04.940
Out with it! Come on, spit it out!

00:15:05.050 --> 00:15:06.410
Spill it!

00:15:07.180 --> 00:15:10.380
All right, I'll talk! Just let me go!

00:15:13.190 --> 00:15:16.560
We will now engage in mock Labor combat.

00:15:16.660 --> 00:15:20.250
Maneuver set 107. No time limit.

00:15:21.060 --> 00:15:23.330
Do it in one shot, Ota!

00:15:24.130 --> 00:15:26.100
Go for it, Kanuka!

00:15:26.940 --> 00:15:28.870
Come on, Ota!

00:15:29.210 --> 00:15:31.670
If you lose, you're not getting any dinner!

00:15:31.780 --> 00:15:35.070
Got it, Ota? You'd better win!

00:15:35.280 --> 00:15:38.610
It happened after your class graduated...

00:15:38.720 --> 00:15:43.210
about two months after the new class of cadets came in.

00:15:44.220 --> 00:15:46.810
They held a public mock combat match...

00:15:46.920 --> 00:15:51.020
coinciding with the conclusion of their first course of study.

00:15:52.060 --> 00:15:57.400
Police big-shots, local officials, and the cadets' families...

00:15:57.500 --> 00:16:00.440
were invited to the school grounds.

00:16:01.140 --> 00:16:06.100
She was sitting at the corner of the tent for the families.

00:16:06.710 --> 00:16:07.680
Begin!

00:16:17.590 --> 00:16:19.490
It happened in the blink of an eye.

00:16:19.590 --> 00:16:21.560
The fallen Labor's gun went off...

00:16:21.660 --> 00:16:24.560
and she was right in front of the muzzle.

00:16:29.500 --> 00:16:32.990
It may have been a practice paint bullet...

00:16:33.100 --> 00:16:36.090
but she never could have survived a hit at that range.

00:16:36.310 --> 00:16:38.640
It was horrible.

00:16:48.750 --> 00:16:49.880
A dud?

00:16:50.250 --> 00:16:51.480
It's the same!

00:16:52.720 --> 00:16:55.950
It's just like what happened back then!

00:17:12.080 --> 00:17:14.640
So what happened next?

00:17:14.740 --> 00:17:15.840
What do you mean?

00:17:15.950 --> 00:17:20.040
I <i>mean</i>, what happened to the cadet who shot her?

00:17:20.720 --> 00:17:22.410
Was he punished?

00:17:22.520 --> 00:17:26.080
This is where it gets ugly.

00:17:26.520 --> 00:17:31.480
They say that the cadet who shot her was her own older brother.

00:17:34.000 --> 00:17:35.690
That's ugly.

00:17:35.800 --> 00:17:37.790
That's what I <i>said</i>!

00:17:39.000 --> 00:17:43.230
Half-crazed, he picked up his sister's body with his Labor...

00:17:43.340 --> 00:17:46.170
and walked all three of them into the lake that night.

00:17:46.280 --> 00:17:49.250
I wonder why a story like that never got out?

00:17:49.350 --> 00:17:51.710
The police have always seen themselves as one big family...

00:17:51.810 --> 00:17:55.250
so it's hard for them to air their dirty laundry in public.

00:17:55.350 --> 00:17:59.190
Pretty much everyone there was an interested party.

00:17:59.290 --> 00:18:04.090
Captains Goto and Nagumo are pretty much cops to the core, too.

00:18:04.260 --> 00:18:06.790
But now everything's connected.

00:18:06.900 --> 00:18:11.200
The waterlogged ghost Labor that was wandering the grounds at night.

00:18:11.300 --> 00:18:14.070
The paint from a paint bullet that got into the bath.

00:18:14.170 --> 00:18:16.330
The girl's ghost that Ota saw.

00:18:16.440 --> 00:18:19.310
And now, the re-occurrence of that tragedy.

00:18:19.410 --> 00:18:22.110
With all that happening to us in just two days...

00:18:22.210 --> 00:18:25.270
maybe all the cadets really ran away.

00:18:25.380 --> 00:18:27.680
Mr. Sakuma's a brave man, all right.

00:18:27.780 --> 00:18:29.410
And a crazy one.

00:18:29.850 --> 00:18:32.220
But why? Why <i>us</i>?

00:18:32.320 --> 00:18:36.020
How come <i>we're</i> cursed? Why's the ghost coming after <i>us</i>?

00:18:36.230 --> 00:18:38.790
Look in a mirror.

00:18:38.900 --> 00:18:40.830
What did <i>I</i> do?

00:18:40.930 --> 00:18:43.590
I didn't fire during that match, anyway!

00:18:43.700 --> 00:18:46.640
I let go of the control grips when I fell over!

00:18:46.740 --> 00:18:49.100
The Labor's finger moved all by itself!

00:18:49.810 --> 00:18:53.900
Looks like we have an answer for whether or not that's true.

00:18:54.910 --> 00:18:56.040
Here he is!

00:18:56.480 --> 00:18:57.710
Shige!

00:19:00.120 --> 00:19:01.610
Thanks!

00:19:05.250 --> 00:19:06.590
Geez, this stuff isn't very good.

00:19:06.690 --> 00:19:08.990
Did you use fresh leaves, or just re-use some old ones?

00:19:09.090 --> 00:19:10.580
So what's the word?

00:19:10.690 --> 00:19:13.220
I'll start with the facts.

00:19:14.800 --> 00:19:18.760
For the moment, let's set aside the hardships I've undergone...

00:19:18.870 --> 00:19:23.170
since arriving here after a long, dangerous, high-speed drive...

00:19:23.270 --> 00:19:27.540
with Officer Izumi; I haven't even had a chance to take a bath.

00:19:27.640 --> 00:19:32.140
Alone, forced to work quickly, I began my hard work to restore...

00:19:32.250 --> 00:19:36.740
Ota's reputation and shed some light on these inexplicable events.

00:19:36.850 --> 00:19:41.260
I ran a check on the entire <i>Labor</i>, not just its startup disk.

00:19:41.860 --> 00:19:45.990
I found a ghost that was left in the Labor's main computer.

00:19:46.100 --> 00:19:47.620
A <i>ghost</i>?

00:19:47.730 --> 00:19:51.630
Somebody tampered with the drive system in the Labor's arm.

00:19:51.730 --> 00:19:55.000
Since I personally checked that Labor before it was loaded onto...

00:19:55.100 --> 00:19:58.230
the trailer, we need to look at the time between then and today.

00:19:58.340 --> 00:20:02.110
You can do that just by altering the program?

00:20:02.210 --> 00:20:05.580
I'd have to give that a <i>very</i> qualified "yes."

00:20:05.680 --> 00:20:07.880
But to actually <i>do</i> it...

00:20:08.250 --> 00:20:12.210
At the SV2, I'm probably the only one who could do it.

00:20:13.360 --> 00:20:15.320
So when do we eat?

00:20:15.430 --> 00:20:19.760
After what happened today, we completely forgot about it.

00:20:19.860 --> 00:20:22.260
What? You haven't made it yet?

00:20:22.370 --> 00:20:27.360
So where's that "Gen" guy? He's gotta be goofing off someplace.

00:20:44.390 --> 00:20:47.080
Good morning, everyone! Thanks for waiting.

00:20:48.290 --> 00:20:51.020
Kanuka isn't here yet.

00:20:51.130 --> 00:20:53.150
That's okay. Let's go ahead and start.

00:20:53.900 --> 00:20:57.990
I suppose you're all wondering why I called you here this morning.

00:20:58.100 --> 00:21:02.630
The time has come to put an end to these "ghost" incidents...

00:21:02.740 --> 00:21:05.370
that have plagued this training school.

00:21:05.480 --> 00:21:06.640
Hey, are you serious?

00:21:06.740 --> 00:21:10.440
Relax. Ghosts just do not exist.

00:21:10.550 --> 00:21:13.240
Would you do the honors, Ms. Watson?

00:21:15.250 --> 00:21:17.980
This is a memorial picture from that public exhibition...

00:21:18.090 --> 00:21:20.520
that we pinched from the Instructors' Room.

00:21:20.620 --> 00:21:21.610
What?

00:21:22.130 --> 00:21:24.490
And this is the victim of that unfortunate accident.

00:21:24.590 --> 00:21:26.990
Unfortunately, we don't know her name.

00:21:27.100 --> 00:21:30.400
And this is Maho Gondo, a 17-year-old girl who's been working...

00:21:30.500 --> 00:21:33.470
part-time at <i>Nakayoshi</i>, a lakeside...

00:21:33.570 --> 00:21:37.340
souvenir shop whose owner I've been friends with.

00:21:37.840 --> 00:21:39.810
Wow! They look exactly alike!

00:21:39.910 --> 00:21:45.850
Officer Izumi and I snuck out last night and took this photo of her.

00:21:46.220 --> 00:21:48.840
I don't think I need to tell you this, Shinohara...

00:21:48.950 --> 00:21:52.390
but if this is just some wild yarn, you won't get off easily.

00:21:53.060 --> 00:21:55.920
We obtained important testimony from Gozo Buchiyama...

00:21:56.030 --> 00:22:00.620
<i>Nakayoshi</i>'s proprietor, concerning the meaning of this resemblance.

00:22:01.730 --> 00:22:05.900
That testimony, which we finally got from a reluctant Mr. Buchiyama...

00:22:06.000 --> 00:22:08.940
upon applying sincere persuasion techniques, was...

00:22:09.270 --> 00:22:11.900
Maho... Maho was such a poor girl.

00:22:12.010 --> 00:22:14.980
We're distantly related, so when her parents died...

00:22:15.080 --> 00:22:18.050
the year she started middle school, I took her in.

00:22:18.150 --> 00:22:21.950
She, her brother, and I lived together after that.

00:22:22.150 --> 00:22:26.450
I have told you about the accident, right?

00:22:27.160 --> 00:22:30.150
Then... the victim of that accident was her...

00:22:30.260 --> 00:22:33.850
Yes. She was Maho's younger sister.

00:22:39.900 --> 00:22:43.740
This may be obvious, but if it weren't for Labor units...

00:22:43.840 --> 00:22:48.140
and if they weren't armed, that accident wouldn't have happened.

00:22:48.240 --> 00:22:53.940
I believe that the girl is acting to point this out.

00:22:54.450 --> 00:22:55.850
Whoa, hold on!

00:22:55.950 --> 00:22:57.040
You've got to be kidding!

00:22:57.490 --> 00:22:59.680
Do you seriously think that a 17-year old girl...

00:22:59.790 --> 00:23:01.950
could write a complex program like that?

00:23:02.160 --> 00:23:06.060
She had an accomplice, a man who hasn't shown himself.

00:23:06.160 --> 00:23:10.290
A man we passed by on the day we got here.

00:23:10.430 --> 00:23:13.330
Gen? You're talking about Gen, aren't you?

00:23:15.240 --> 00:23:18.260
These are abandoned items we confiscated from his room.

00:23:18.370 --> 00:23:19.840
Ready?

00:23:20.040 --> 00:23:22.140
A magazine for data processing specialists.

00:23:22.250 --> 00:23:24.240
An empty paint bullet cartridge.

00:23:24.350 --> 00:23:26.110
A skull mask.

00:23:27.050 --> 00:23:29.570
And the <i>piece de</i> <i>resistance:</i> this tape!

00:23:31.020 --> 00:23:33.750
Don't shoot...

00:23:33.860 --> 00:23:38.190
Please, don't shoot...

00:23:39.100 --> 00:23:41.690
Further investigation into the connection...

00:23:41.800 --> 00:23:43.990
between those two people will have to wait...

00:23:44.100 --> 00:23:48.800
but up until 50 years ago, Japanese police weren't armed.

00:23:48.900 --> 00:23:52.500
I won't reiterate the rules of their handling here...

00:23:52.610 --> 00:23:58.050
but I believe this incident is to make us rethink what guns are for...

00:23:58.150 --> 00:24:01.480
as well as to make us reflect on our actions.

00:24:02.080 --> 00:24:05.420
So are they gonna be arrested, Captain?

00:24:08.690 --> 00:24:10.450
No one's going to be arrested.

00:24:10.990 --> 00:24:12.050
Kanuka!

00:24:12.860 --> 00:24:17.060
Even if we tried to, this "Gen" isn't anywhere to be found...

00:24:17.170 --> 00:24:20.660
and the accident victim's older sister doesn't exist, either.

00:24:20.770 --> 00:24:23.710
Not only that, the mock combat accident that happened...

00:24:23.810 --> 00:24:27.040
two months ago is itself a completely fictitious event.

00:24:27.580 --> 00:24:31.010
Hey! What do you mean? How about explaining that?

00:24:31.110 --> 00:24:34.510
When you're uncertain, you should always start by questioning...

00:24:34.620 --> 00:24:36.640
any information that is <i>handed</i> to you.

00:24:36.750 --> 00:24:39.080
If you examine the possibilities that follow <i>only</i> from...

00:24:39.190 --> 00:24:41.620
that which you have personally seen and experienced...

00:24:41.720 --> 00:24:43.620
you'll always arrive at the truth.

00:24:43.830 --> 00:24:46.020
Circumstantial evidence, unsubstantiated testimony...

00:24:46.130 --> 00:24:47.990
and those too-convenient abandoned items.

00:24:48.100 --> 00:24:50.790
All of these hinge upon one supposition:

00:24:50.900 --> 00:24:53.530
That is, the existence of the accident...

00:24:53.640 --> 00:24:55.760
two months ago and the man named Gen.

00:24:55.870 --> 00:25:00.400
What if Mr. Gen never existed in the first place?

00:25:00.510 --> 00:25:04.810
What if the mock combat exposition concluded uneventfully?

00:25:04.910 --> 00:25:07.410
What if the girl in the photo and the part-timer...

00:25:07.520 --> 00:25:09.540
were one and the same?

00:25:09.850 --> 00:25:12.050
Let's start with the alleged Mr. Gen.

00:25:12.620 --> 00:25:14.320
I'll get the mud out of your uniforms...

00:25:14.420 --> 00:25:16.080
so leave them out once you're done.

00:25:16.660 --> 00:25:18.850
Right, you wouldn't know him.

00:25:18.960 --> 00:25:22.660
Mr. Gen there is an all-around handyman now.

00:25:22.770 --> 00:25:25.730
He appeared unexpectedly, and we were made to play along...

00:25:25.840 --> 00:25:27.500
by someone especially trustworthy.

00:25:27.600 --> 00:25:29.370
Since no one has actually <i>seen</i> him...

00:25:29.470 --> 00:25:32.600
this makes him a very suspicious character.

00:25:33.310 --> 00:25:36.240
He is a fictional character, created by Captain Goto's voice...

00:25:36.350 --> 00:25:38.610
with Captain Nagumo in a co-starring role.

00:25:38.710 --> 00:25:42.080
And he also never helped out with the cooking.

00:25:42.690 --> 00:25:44.480
And now, the two girls:

00:25:44.590 --> 00:25:46.280
If you didn't know about the accident...

00:25:46.390 --> 00:25:49.220
you'd assume that they were the same person.

00:25:49.330 --> 00:25:52.350
Because we were told that the girl in the picture had died...

00:25:52.460 --> 00:25:55.950
we were easily taken in by the lie that they were sisters.

00:25:56.070 --> 00:25:59.230
The very fact that she is still alive provides irrefutable proof...

00:25:59.340 --> 00:26:02.100
that the accident two months ago never happened.

00:26:03.110 --> 00:26:05.400
As for the mock combat program, it's quite simple.

00:26:05.640 --> 00:26:09.540
As Shige said, only <i>he</i> could write such a complex program.

00:26:09.650 --> 00:26:12.640
It follows, then, that Shige himself did it.

00:26:13.180 --> 00:26:17.080
Mr. Sakuma is, of course, a collaborator.

00:26:18.120 --> 00:26:20.550
To sum up, everything was a fabrication...

00:26:20.660 --> 00:26:24.020
made up by everyone <i>except</i> the squad members.

00:26:24.330 --> 00:26:25.760
The trusted superior officers.

00:26:25.860 --> 00:26:27.830
The tough instructor from your cadet days.

00:26:27.930 --> 00:26:29.420
The old store-owner friend.

00:26:29.530 --> 00:26:31.690
The young girl with the sad eyes.

00:26:32.070 --> 00:26:34.540
People whom you'd never suspect of lying...

00:26:34.640 --> 00:26:37.540
came together to tell the same lie. That was your blind spot.

00:26:38.140 --> 00:26:40.630
They started off by making you believe in ghosts...

00:26:40.740 --> 00:26:45.440
and then made it more believable by denying it themselves.

00:26:45.710 --> 00:26:49.450
You divulge a little lie to hide a larger one.

00:26:49.820 --> 00:26:52.790
Even if you know that magic tricks and mystery books use the same...

00:26:52.890 --> 00:26:56.050
method, if it develops to where you're actually drawn in, you...

00:26:56.160 --> 00:26:59.320
unknowingly lose sight of the truth and your judgement is clouded.

00:26:59.560 --> 00:27:02.790
You follow the map according to a plot that's already been scripted...

00:27:02.900 --> 00:27:05.030
you collect the concocted testimony and items...

00:27:05.130 --> 00:27:08.630
and all you do is reach a fake goal that you yourself created.

00:27:09.040 --> 00:27:10.770
But why? What for?

00:27:10.870 --> 00:27:13.310
You said it yourself:

00:27:13.880 --> 00:27:19.820
To make us re-think how we use guns and make us reflect on our actions.

00:27:20.880 --> 00:27:23.440
I understand your intentions, Captain...

00:27:23.550 --> 00:27:25.140
but I don't approve of your methods!

00:27:26.720 --> 00:27:29.690
Your deductive work has been very interesting, Kanuka...

00:27:29.790 --> 00:27:33.420
but since you've got no hard evidence, same as Asuma...

00:27:33.530 --> 00:27:35.090
it's all just supposition, isn't it?

00:27:35.200 --> 00:27:36.260
Come on in.

00:27:39.770 --> 00:27:41.600
Allow me to reintroduce our guest.

00:27:41.700 --> 00:27:45.040
This is Mahoko Goto. Captain Goto's <i>niece</i>.

00:27:45.140 --> 00:27:46.270
Hello!

00:27:47.940 --> 00:27:52.380
Sorry, Uncle! She was too good! I spilled the beans!

00:27:55.750 --> 00:27:56.780
Sorry.

00:27:58.520 --> 00:28:00.820
- Die!
- Don't!

00:28:01.720 --> 00:28:03.450
Please! Don't!

00:28:04.630 --> 00:28:06.120
Don't shoot...

00:28:14.460 --> 00:28:18.670
The Tragedy of L

00:29:15.920 --> 00:29:18.440
Mysterious men spy on the Labor hangar!

00:29:18.550 --> 00:29:20.920
An armed Labor forces its way through a checkpoint!

00:29:21.020 --> 00:29:23.420
But the Second Unit's away on vacation!

00:29:23.790 --> 00:29:25.780
Something's happening in a snowy Tokyo!

00:29:25.890 --> 00:29:27.690
Noa! Let's go to Tokyo!

00:29:27.790 --> 00:29:30.760
Next time! " The SV2's Longest Day: Part One"!

00:29:30.860 --> 00:29:32.690
Target, lock on!
